course: dictionary
lesson: 1701
title: Churchyard: the land around a church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A churchyard is the land around a church. Often it has a graveyard, where people are buried, so you may see gravestones there. When you meet this word, look at the words around it to work out where the story is set.
explain: «In a burial the coffin is lowered into a grave in a cemetery or churchyard.» The words coffin, grave and burial are clues. A churchyard is one of the places where a burial can happen, so it must be a place with graves.
explain: In stories, a churchyard is often a quiet place, and sometimes a spooky one. Gravestones, old trees and walls create the feeling. Ask yourself: what does the author want me to feel here? Quiet, calm or frightened?
fact: A churchyard is the land around a church, often with a graveyard.
fact: «Yews can live well over a thousand years, and some in British churchyards are among the oldest trees in Europe.»
fact: Gravestones in churchyards can tell historians about people of the past, such as their names, ages and families.
fact: In ghost stories, a churchyard is a quiet, sometimes spooky place with gravestones, trees and old walls.
exercise: What is a churchyard? | *The land around a church, often with a graveyard | A type of river boat | A shop that sells candles | A tall tower that rings bells
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Yews can live well over a thousand years, and some in British churchyards are among the oldest trees in Europe.» that names a type of tree. | churchyards | *yews | Europe | oldest
exercise: In history lessons, what can gravestones in a churchyard tell us? | How to cook a meal | *The names, ages and families of people from the past | The weather last week | How fast cars can go
test: In a ghost story, what does a churchyard usually feel like? | *A quiet, sometimes spooky place with gravestones, trees and old walls | A busy shopping street | A river full of boats | A loud fairground
test: Why might a writer set a scene in a churchyard at night? | Because churchyards sell food | Because there are swimming pools there | Because it is full of noisy children | *Because gravestones, old walls and quiet make the scene feel spooky
exam: Which word in «a grave in a cemetery or churchyard» names a place that is most like a churchyard? | *cemetery | grave | coffin | lowered
